m2_alpha_llm: the s1_alpha_llm mission as a small fleet.

One shoreside community (MOOSDB 9000, pShare 9200) runs pMarineViewer with
the chat pane and pLLMAgent. Each simulated vehicle (abe, ben, ... on
9001+/9201+) is its own community with the blank alpha helm and its own
pBehaviorTree. The model names a vehicle (or all) in every tool;
uFldShoreBroker carries DEPLOY_ABE, BT_TREE_ABE and friends down to abe as
the bare variables, and each vehicle's uFldNodeBroker sends its node
report, its plan's map shapes and its status back up renamed with its
name (BT_STATE_ABE, BT_CHAT_ABE, MISSION_ABE); pLLMAgent and the chat pane
route by that suffix.

  ./launch.sh [--amt=N] [--nogui] [--just_make] [time_warp]

launch.sh runs launch_vehicle.sh once per vehicle and launch_shoreside.sh,
filling meta_vehicle.moos, meta_vehicle.bhv and meta_shoreside.moos with
nsplug (the targ_* files are the results), then runs uMAC on the
shoreside; quitting uMAC or Ctrl-C halts everything. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
must be set in the shell for the chat to answer; without it the fleet
still runs from the viewer's buttons (they act on every vehicle; there is
no mouse context) and from uPokeDB.

The shoreside also runs uFldSquad (moos-ivp-squad): squads of vehicles as
objects. SQUAD_CMD forms a squad (its members take the squad color on the
map), moves its center of mass with every member keeping its offset, or
puts it in a formation (line, column, wedge, circle ...) that holds at rest
and moves as a body behind a virtual leader the members trail with
BHV_Trail (the formation block in meta_vehicle.bhv). SQUAD_REPORT_<NAME>,
SQUAD_<NAME>_X/_Y/... and SQUAD_MISSION_<NAME> come back. pLLMAgent gets the
squad_* tools from the squad capability set (a capability_dir = squad line),
and the contact set (capability_dir = contact): follow, one vehicle
trailing another along its exact track at a set distance, through the
BHV_Convoy block in meta_vehicle.bhv (TASK = convoy, CONVOY_UPDATE);
intercept, one vehicle chasing another at a given top speed and closing
to within a range, through the BHV_CutRange block (TASK = intercept,
INTERCEPT_UPDATE) and a BHV_MaxSpeed block on the same task
(INTERCEPT_SPEED_UPDATE; the cut-range behavior would otherwise run at
the helm's 4 m/s and coast through the range); the behavior never
completes, so the plan leaf ends on the executor's own contact range and
its finish line idles the helm, while a tool call runs until the next
command; and avoid, the vehicle's collision avoidance,
colregs (BHV_AvdColregsV22) or basic (BHV_AvoidCollision) or off, one
AVOID flag the two templated blocks condition on. pContactMgrV20 on each
vehicle spawns those per contact (ignore_type = virtual keeps them off a
squad's leader) and every vehicle starts with AVOID = off; on, the 20 m
standoff (max_util_cpa_dist) is what a follow or an intercept cannot get
inside, unless avoid_ignore leaves that one contact out (BHV_ABLE_FILTER,
qbridged; avoid_heed takes it back) (headless at warp 10: a crossing with it off collided, with it on
passed at 13 to 17 m; a 20 m line formation moved with its members 23 m
apart and a 20 m follow settled 29 m behind). uFldCollisionDetect on the shoreside counts encounters, near
misses (8 m) and collisions (4 m) between vehicles: COLLISION and
NEAR_MISS name the pair and the _TOTAL variables count. pLLMAgent pushes
the two events to the model as [alert: ...] notes, each opening a turn
of its own so the agent can report and propose (alert = COLLISION,
NEAR_MISS), off at launch; LLM_ALERTS=on, from the viewer's Action menu
or uPokeDB, turns them on and off mutes them again. Also
from that run: uFldSquad's slot legs set a member's waypoint speed to
1.2 m/s and the helm keeps it, so a member let go (formation_off, stop,
disband) now gets release_speed back.

Beside it runs one pBehaviorTree with a plan slot per squad (squads_var =
SQUAD_LIST): a squad's variables carry its suffix (BT_TREE_RED, BT_STATE_RED,
BT_CHAT_RED, BT_PLAN_RED ...), so a plan reaches red the way a vehicle's
reaches abe, two squads run two plans at once, and a disbanded squad's plan
is halted with it. A plan for vehicles not yet in a squad forms it: its
first step is SquadForm, and both the executor and pLLMAgent take the new
name (plans/squad_form_line.xml). A squad plan starts with a bare <Squad> (the whole squad,
from SQUAD_REPORT_<NAME>) and drives no vehicle itself: each Member block,
or a leaf with a vname, goes down to that vehicle as its own plan and the
block waits on BT_STATE_<VNAME>; Report lines come back up as
BT_REPORT_<VNAME>, and back down to every vehicle under that name
(bridge = src=BT_REPORT_* in the broker block), so two vehicles' own
plans can wait on each other's milestone instead of a position test that
goes false the moment the other moves on; each vehicle's VEHICLE_FACTS
(cruise, speed limit, return point, slip radius from the helm's own
posts, the avoidance standoff typed once as STANDOFF in launch_vehicle.sh
for the .bhv blocks and the executor's fact line, and the measured
dynamics from uDynamicsTest's dyn/<vname>.txt: turning radius, stopping
distance, acceleration distance and turn rate per speed, through the
executor's facts_from) comes up as VEHICLE_FACTS_<VNAME> and pLLMAgent
puts them in its prompt, so prompts/fleet.txt states no number the
system publishes; Signal goes down as BT_SIGNAL; the squad leaves
(SquadFormation, SquadGoto ...) run on the executor and post SQUAD_CMD. The
squad's report shows the plan (plan=, plan_state=). pLLMAgent learns the
squads from SQUAD_LIST too (run_plan vname=red) and the fleet prompt tells
the model to form a squad, then plan for it. Vehicles a plan does not list
are left alone; a member taken out of its squad is taken over, and the squad
plan ends. plans/squad_wedge_south.xml is a plan of squad leaves (form a
wedge, move south), plans/squad_line_south.xml the full Member form (each
member reports at the line, the coordinator signals the move south),
plans/squad_box.xml the compact form, plans/follow_ben.xml a vehicle
reacting to another through the contact variables (BEN_RANGE). A member
may itself be a squad (a squad of squads; see the moos-ivp-bt README), which
this mission keeps out to stay minimal.

uPlanPreview (moos-ivp-bt) also runs on the shoreside: while a proposal
waits for y/n, pLLMAgent posts it as PLAN_PREVIEW (preview_var) and
phantom boats play it out on the map from the boats' current positions,
ten plan seconds per second, a dot per vehicle in its proposal color
with its name and the words of any step that is not a movement beside
it ("abe: Say 'done'", "red: waiting for abe"), replayed until the
proposal resolves. A plan file can be previewed by hand:
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos 'PLAN_PREVIEW:=<preview><plan owner="red" file="plans/squad_box.xml"/></preview>'
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos PLAN_PREVIEW:=none
Straight lines and instant turns, no avoidance: it shows the plan's logic
and geometry, not the helm's dynamics.

uButtonPanel (moos-ivp-panel) is the operator's button panel, its own
window beside the viewer: one button per block of buttons.txt in this
directory. STOP ALL is written by hand there and posts the same flags as
the viewer's button; the rest are the agent's. Asked for a button in the
chat ("make a button called GO HOME that sends abe home"), the model
calls make_button with a label, an owner and a plan; the proposal shows
the plan's steps, and on y pLLMAgent writes the block to buttons.txt
(buttons_file in its config block), the panel re-reads the file and shows
it, and each press posts LLM_BUTTON=GO HOME, on which pLLMAgent posts the
saved plan to abe's executor as an approved run_plan would, no model
call. The same label again replaces the button, "remove the GO HOME
button" deletes it, and the file is plain text to edit by hand (both
apps re-read it when it changes); the buttons stay from launch to launch
and belong to this mission. Without the model a saved button still
works, from the panel or by hand:
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos 'LLM_BUTTON:=GO HOME'

Without the model, from this directory:
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos BT_TREE_FILE_ABE=plans/box_goto.xml
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos TASK_BEN=waypoint WPT_UPDATE_BEN=points=40,-40 DEPLOY_BEN=true MOOS_MANUAL_OVERRIDE_BEN=false
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos BT_REPLY_ABE=yes
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos SQUAD_CMD:=action=create,name=red,members=abe:ben
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos BT_TREE_FILE_RED=plans/squad_wedge_south.xml
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos BT_CMD_RED=halt
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos BT_CMD_ALL=halt
  uXMS targ_shoreside.moos BT_STATE_RED BT_PLAN_RED BT_MEMBERS_RED BT_STATE_ABE BT_STATE_BEN BT_REPORT_ABE BT_REPORT_BEN
  pBehaviorTree --check=plans/squad_line_south.xml --squad --roster=abe,ben
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos SQUAD_CMD:=action=formation,name=red,shape=line,spacing=30
  uPokeDB targ_shoreside.moos SQUAD_CMD:=action=goto,name=red,x=60,y=-160
  uXMS targ_shoreside.moos SQUAD_LIST SQUAD_REPORT_RED SQUAD_MISSION_RED SQUAD_EVENT

This is the shape the MCTF mission takes later: pLLMAgent joins its
shoreside block, pBehaviorTree and the bridge lines join meta_surveyor.moos.
